# SYNOPSIS

```c
#include <strings.h>

int strcasecmp(const char *s1, const char *s2);
int strncasecmp(const char *s1, const char *s2, size_t n);
```

# DESCRIPTION

`strcasecmp` compares the strings <s1> and <s2> as `strcmp` of string(2) does, after mapping each `A` to `Z` to lower case.
`strncasecmp` compares at most <n> bytes.
Each returns zero if the strings are equal, otherwise the difference of the first two bytes that differ, as unsigned values folded to lower case.

Only ASCII letters are folded: the locale is "C".

